Lighthouse: licence for prose and derived data

What this covers. Lighthouse's own writing (pieces, essays, records, notes,
investigation and site pages) and the data Lighthouse derives itself (tables,
tabulations, figures and other outputs its scripts compute) are licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribute as "Lighthouse (https://lighthouse.harbour.cat)", naming the piece or
record and its version where you can, and say if you changed it.

What it does not cover. Material Lighthouse retains from third parties (raw
reads, fetched pages and response bodies, downloaded datasets, quoted
documents, and anything else collected from outside sources, most of it under
studies/*/data/) stays under its owners' terms. Lighthouse keeps it as evidence
and grants no licence to it. Quotations in Lighthouse's writing are used for
reporting and remain their authors'.

Code. Scripts and site code are under the MIT licence in LICENSE.

